Interactive edits of the instances of a mesh light authored with primvars:arnold:light

see #2193 and #2437

A grey wall is only lit by the two instances of a small mesh light, moved in front of the wall by the prototype's own
transform. The intensity of the mesh light is edited, an instance is moved, the mesh light is disabled and enabled
again, then the prototype is moved. Each instance must light the wall from its instance and prototype transforms, and
the prototype light itself, in front of the center of the wall, must not emit.
The scenario runs with the "usd" procedural reading the stage through its cache_id in an interactive render session,
and with the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra host, see
testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the initial procedural render is
compared against the reference image. The legacy usd reader doesn't instance these mesh lights yet, the test is
skipped in the 'usd' pass (see the testsuite groups). As for the other instanced lights (e.g. with the MeshLightAPI),
the light instances rebuilt by an interactive update of the procedural with the hydra reader aren't rendered, this is
reported as a known issue.

author: cyril.pichard

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
